WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.990
- I have something funny though.

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:03.810
So, when you told your mom who
loves to cook soulful food,

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.950
like soul food.
- [Common] Yeah.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.290
- That you were gonna be a vegan,

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.095
how'd that go over?

00:00:09.095 --> 00:00:11.100
Was she like, "Wait, what?"

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:11.933
- Well, first of all,

00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:13.890
she was like, "What
are you talking about?"

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.130
Like, when I didn't want to
eat the turkey at Thanksgiving.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:17.963
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:17.963 --> 00:00:19.650
- And the foods that I normally ate,

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:20.820
they were in shock.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.640
She was kind of like, she
felt like I rejected her

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.540
and I understand

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.640
'cause that was her way
of giving love, you know?

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.473
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:27.473 --> 00:00:28.317
- Her son is coming home, I'm
working all over the time.

00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:30.090
- And she spent a minute on that turkey.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.260
- She spent a minute on that.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.404
She cooked the greens.

00:00:32.404 --> 00:00:35.880
But once she saw I was for
real about it, you know,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.680
the next year, the next year,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.610
then it was like, okay,

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.670
I gotta start cooking some
vegetarian food for this guy.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.020
And she did it

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.967
and it wasn't that good
at first, you know?

00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:46.080
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.250
That's like me trying to bake

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:48.870
with all the like healthy sugars.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:49.703
I'm like.

00:00:49.703 --> 00:00:51.240
- Yeah, you gotta learn how to.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.180
- Yeah.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.013
- You gotta learn how to still--

00:00:53.013 --> 00:00:53.940
- The chemistry of that, yeah.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.860
- Now, let me say, because
I know my mother's watching,

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.205
she has improved.
(audience laughs)

00:00:59.205 --> 00:01:00.705
She's a very good.

00:01:02.844 --> 00:01:04.561
- Your mama is gonna whoop your ass.

00:01:04.561 --> 00:01:05.476
(Common laughs)

00:01:05.476 --> 00:01:06.309
- She's a very good.

00:01:06.309 --> 00:01:08.720
- She's like, "I have improved, okay."

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.290
- She's good, she's really good now.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.123
- Do you cook?

00:01:11.123 --> 00:01:11.956
Do you like cooking?

00:01:11.956 --> 00:01:13.020
- No, I don't cook at all.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:13.903
- I know.

00:01:13.903 --> 00:01:14.736
I don't think

00:01:14.736 --> 00:01:16.818
you could be judging other
people's skills then.

00:01:16.818 --> 00:01:18.477
- Still I know what tastes good,

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:19.310
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.143
- I'm like, look, I was like,

00:01:20.143 --> 00:01:20.976
"You know what this tastes like,

00:01:20.976 --> 00:01:23.130
"I didn't cook it, so
I'll put it in my mouth."

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.484
- Are you a good chef?

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.830
- No.
(audience laughs)

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:26.663
No.

